{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "anisotropic_diffusion_2d_neumann",
    "description": "MMS driver: forced-steady anisotropic diffusion on the unit box [0,1]x[0,1] with homogeneous NEUMANN (zero-normal-gradient) walls, the vehicle that exercises grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_Dxy_neumann_bc (the mixed second derivative d^2u/dx dy off-diagonal term). WHY THE ANISOTROPIC HOST: the isolated discrete cross operator is symmetric INDEFINITE (eigenvalues -N^2..+N^2), so a bare cross derivative is not a stable time-evolution operator; it IS the off-diagonal term of a positive-definite anisotropic diffusion tensor K = [[Kxx, Kxy], [Kxy, Kyy]]. This problem takes Kxx = Kyy = 1, Kxy = 1/2 (2 Kxy = 1), discretizing L = D(D(u,x),x) + D(D(u,x),y) + D(D(u,y),y) via central_D2x_neumann_bc + central_Dxy_neumann_bc + central_D2y_neumann_bc (three priority-10 compound rules superposing). WELL-POSEDNESS CAVEAT (Neumann is subtler than Dirichlet): the energy estimate is d/dt (1/2)||u||^2 = c(-integral grad u . K grad u + boundary integral of u (n.K grad u)). For the anisotropic tensor the natural stable wall condition is the CONORMAL n.K grad u = 0, but the per-axis rules impose the plain normal derivative (du/dx=0 on x-walls, du/dy=0 on y-walls); the conormal then retains the cross term n.K grad u = Kxy u_tangential on each wall, so the boundary integral is of indefinite sign and L is not provably negative definite (contrast the Dirichlet problem, whose vanishing wall value kills the boundary term outright). The combined operator is therefore only conditionally well-posed as an evolution: a general roundoff perturbation can excite the residual boundary flux. For the chosen u* = cos(pi x) cos(pi y) the boundary integral vanishes identically (u^2 takes equal values at the wall endpoints / corners), and the strongly dissipative diagonal bulk keeps the integration stable through t=0.1 at the tested resolutions - the observed drift is the pure O(dx^2+dy^2) truncation. MANUFACTURED STEADY SOLUTION u*(x,y) = cos(pi x) cos(pi y), which has zero normal derivative on all four walls (compatible with homogeneous Neumann qXL=qXR=qYL=qYR=0) and whose exact even extension about each wall is reproduced by the cell-centered even-reflection ghost, held steady by the analytic forcing c*S with S = -L[u*] = 2 pi^2 cos(pi x) cos(pi y) - pi^2 sin(pi x) sin(pi y) (L[u*] = u*_xx + u*_xy + u*_yy = -pi^2 cc - pi^2 cc + pi^2 ss). The continuous balance u_t = c(L u* - L u*) = 0 holds, so the discrete field drifts only by the O(dx^2 + dy^2) truncation of L, whose cross-derivative half is central_Dxy_neumann_bc. Geometry contract for the unit box: x0=y0=0, dx=1/NX, dy=1/NY (observeds dividing by the metaparameter names, substituted as integer literals at load per esm-spec 9.7.6). BUILD-TIME SCOPE CAVEAT (AGENTS.md): the ic, forcing observed S, and test references spell the cell-center coordinates x_i = (i-1/2)/NX, y_j = (j-1/2)/NY inline from literals and NX,NY, never invoking the grid's x_coord/y_coord free-name templates. NOTE the four Neumann wall fluxes qXL/qXR/qYL/qYR are consumed ONLY by the diagonal central_D2x/D2y_neumann_bc rules; central_Dxy_neumann_bc carries no wall free names because a constant-along-wall flux cancels in the tangential difference of the mixed derivative (see that rule's description).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "equation:diffusion",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.12 (mixed partial derivatives; cell-centered Neumann even-reflection ghost) and Chapter 3 (multidimensional operators)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "AnisotropicDiffusion2DNeumann": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D2x_neumann_bc.esm"
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_Dxy_neumann_bc.esm"
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D2y_neumann_bc.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "Diffused scalar field over the 2-D [x, y] index sets."
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Scalar diffusivity multiplying the whole anisotropic operator AND the whole forcing, so the steady MMS balance c(L u* + S)=0 holds for any c>0 (and c>0 keeps the bulk of L dissipative)."
        },
        "qXL": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K/m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "df/dx at the left x-wall (central_D2x_neumann_bc free name). Homogeneous 0: u* = cos(pi x) cos(pi y) has zero x-derivative on x=0."
        },
        "qXR": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K/m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "df/dx at the right x-wall. Homogeneous 0: u* has zero x-derivative on x=1."
        },
        "qYL": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K/m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "df/dy at the bottom y-wall (central_D2y_neumann_bc free name). Homogeneous 0: u* has zero y-derivative on y=0."
        },
        "qYR": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K/m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "df/dy at the top y-wall. Homogeneous 0: u* has zero y-derivative on y=1."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left x domain edge a = 0 (unit box): the grid's x0 free name (grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "y0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Bottom y domain edge b = 0 (unit box): the grid's y0 free name."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "x-spacing 1/NX: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the expanded rule bodies at evaluation. NX is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6) so the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "dy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "y-spacing 1/NY: the grid's dy free name; NY substituted at load so the sweep keeps dy consistent."
        },
        "S": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "Analytic steady forcing S = -L[u*] with L[u*] = u*_xx + u*_xy + u*_yy (Kxx=Kyy=1, 2 Kxy=1). Constant in time; c*S holds u* steady. Coordinates spelled inline from literals and NX, NY (build-time scope caveat). pi^2 = 9.869604401089358; 2 pi^2 = 19.739208802178716."
        }
      },
